## Vercel Speed Insights Installation - Complete

I have successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this static HTML website.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Created `package.json` in the public directory
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- Generated `package-lock.json` for dependency locking

#### 2. Speed Insights Integration
Added Speed Insights tracking scripts to all HTML pages:
- `index.html` - Main homepage
- `about.html` - About page
- `contact.html` - Contact page
- `disclaimer.html` - Disclaimer page
- `privacy-policy.html` - Privacy policy page
- `admin/index.html` - Admin panel page

#### 3. Implementation Details
For each HTML file, I added the following script tags just before the closing `</head>` tag:

```html
<script>
  window.si = window.si || function () { (window.siq = window.siq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js"></script>
```

This follows the official Vercel documentation for static HTML sites. The script:
- Initializes the Speed Insights queue (`window.si`)
- Loads the Speed Insights script asynchronously from `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js`
- Uses `defer` to ensure it doesn't block page rendering

#### 4. Git Configuration
- Created `.gitignore` to exclude `node_modules/` and other build artifacts from version control

### How It Works

1. **Automatic Script Loading**: When deployed on Vercel, the `/_vercel/speed-insights/script.js` path will automatically be served by Vercel's infrastructure
2. **Real User Monitoring**: Speed Insights will collect real user performance metrics including:
   - Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
   - First Contentful Paint (FCP)
   - Time to First Byte (TTFB)
3. **Dashboard Access**: Metrics will be available in your Vercel project dashboard under the Speed Insights section

### Deployment Steps

1. The changes are ready to be deployed to Vercel
2. After deployment, enable Speed Insights in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Metrics will start appearing after users visit your site

### Technical Notes

- **Framework**: Static HTML (no framework)
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Integration Method**: Script tag injection (recommended for static HTML sites)
- **Script Loading**: Deferred to avoid blocking page rendering
- **All Pages Covered**: Speed Insights is now active on all 6 HTML pages

The implementation follows the latest Vercel documentation fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart and uses the recommended approach for static HTML websites.
